     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br><br>Em sábado, 20 de janeiro de 2018 01:27:15 UTC-2, <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">kma...@aol.com</a>  escreveu:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"color:blue;white-space:pre\"><div style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px;white-space:normal\"><pre style=\"font-family:&quot;Ubuntu Mono&quot;;outline:none;border-width:initial;border-style:none;word-break:break-all;line-height:14.5455px;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-size:10.4pt!important;white-space:pre-wrap!important\">Elias,<br>  I suppose that you could bootstrap the desired standard errors and then divide the raw residuals by the resulting standard error estimates.  You can use &#39;/&#39; to divide each element in a matrix by the corresponding element of a matrix of equal dimensions.<b><br><br></b><div style=\"font-weight:bold;background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> A </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> matrix</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">seq</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">8</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#008\">by</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> ncol</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> nrow</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> B </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> matrix</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> ncol</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> nrow</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> A<br>     </span><span style=\"color:#660\">[,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">[,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,]</span><span style=\"color:#000\">    </span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#000\">    </span><span style=\"color:#066\">6</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,]</span><span style=\"color:#000\">    </span><span style=\"color:#066\">4</span><span style=\"color:#000\">    </span><span style=\"color:#066\">8</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> B<br>     </span><span style=\"color:#660\">[,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">[,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,]</span><span style=\"color:#000\">    </span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#000\">    </span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,]</span><span style=\"color:#000\">    </span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#000\">    </span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> A </span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> B<br>     </span><span style=\"color:#660\">[,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">[,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,]</span><span style=\"color:#000\">    </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#000\">    </span><span style=\"color:#066\">3</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,]</span><span style=\"color:#000\">    </span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#000\">    </span><span style=\"color:#066\">4</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span></div></code></div><b><br></b></pre></div></span></div></blockquote><div><br></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div><b>Can you post an practical example using lavaan?</b></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div> </div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"color:blue;white-space:pre\"><div style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px;white-space:normal\"><pre style=\"font-family:&quot;Ubuntu Mono&quot;;outline:none;border-width:initial;border-style:none;word-break:break-all;line-height:14.5455px;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-size:10.4pt!important;white-space:pre-wrap!important\">Bear in mind that you are performing multiple tests.  So, alpha = .05 may not serve you well with standardized or normalized residuals.  </pre></div></span></div></blockquote><div><br></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div><b>You mean the alpha for resid command in lavaan is 0.05? The help of this command does not show much information about it.</b></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div> </div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"color:blue;white-space:pre\"><div style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px;white-space:normal\"><pre style=\"font-family:&quot;Ubuntu Mono&quot;;outline:none;border-width:initial;border-style:none;word-break:break-all;line-height:14.5455px;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-size:10.4pt!important;white-space:pre-wrap!important\">Personally, I prefer to simply place the correlation residuals into a stem-and-leaf plot and look for outliers or residuals above a size that I deem practically significant.<br></pre></div></span></div></blockquote><div><br></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div>Good idea, so again, would you give a practical example, I search for this kind of graph but need to understand better how to apply it</div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div> </div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"color:blue;white-space:pre\"><div style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px;white-space:normal\"><pre style=\"font-family:&quot;Ubuntu Mono&quot;;outline:none;border-width:initial;border-style:none;word-break:break-all;line-height:14.5455px;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-size:10.4pt!important;white-space:pre-wrap!important\"><br>Keith<br>------------------------<br>Keith A. Markus<br>John Jay College of Criminal Justice, CUNY<br><a href=\"http://jjcweb.jjay.cuny.edu/kmarkus\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://jjcweb.jjay.cuny.edu/kmarkus&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792426153951000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3wkuRvxbEI-HwVliPcE7NV\">http://jjcweb.jjay.cuny.edu/kmarkus</a><br>Frontiers of Test Validity Theory: Measurement, Causation and Meaning.<br><a href=\"http://www.routledge.com/books/details/9781841692203/\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.routledge.com/books/details/9781841692203/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792426153951000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0Zdn1AFfN8viZMEZVqykH1\">http://www.routledge.com/books/details/9781841692203/</a><br><br><br><br><br><br>\r\n</pre></div></span></div></blockquote></div></div>"
